    "visualReview": "Parent Read inspected corrected body concept four views, runtime idle/walk/special, eight consecutive movement/display closeups, five unobstructed opposing views, head/wing-root/leg-root/dorsal details, 390/800 playing cards, and actual 390/1440 source glyph crops. Single snake head, complete scaled body and tapered tail, six articulated legs and four feather wings are visible. Gray umber reticulation and dark eyes remain readable after the offline palette correction. Sampled frames show attached roots, no evident stretching strands or detached appendages. The exact source glyph 𧔥 is visibly rendered; Chrome platform font evidence confirms one glyph from Shanhai Rare Han and the remaining source glyphs from Songti SC. Counts and numerical QA do not substitute for this image review.",
